<!-- Yesim Content -->
<div class="content-section">

  {% set primary = provider.codes | findCode(provider.primaryCode) %}
  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>Best Yesim Promo Code &bull; {{ buildMonthYear }}</h2>
    <p>
      Use <strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong> for <strong>{{ primary.discount | lower }}</strong>. It's a public code, not one of ours (Yesim doesn't run an affiliate program of the kind that would let us have our own code here), but it's the best one we've verified.
      <span class="callout-meta">Confirmed active <time datetime="{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtISO }}">{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtDate("MMM d, yyyy") }}</time>.</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Headline -->
  <h2>What Actually Makes Yesim Different</h2>
  <p>
    Most eSIM apps on this site sell you a fixed block of data and that's the end of the relationship until you buy again. Yesim's "Pay & Fly" plans work more like a prepaid balance: you buy data in dollars rather than gigabytes, it's priced from $1.10/GB, and whatever you don't use rolls over instead of expiring the moment your trip ends. If you're a frequent flyer who tops up the same balance trip after trip rather than buying a fresh block every time, that's a genuinely different model from the fixed-GB or fixed-day plans <a href="/airhub/">Airhub</a> and most other providers here sell.
  </p>
  <p>
    Yesim also advertises automatic network switching (they call it "SwitchLess Networks") across a claimed 800+ partner networks, so the eSIM hops to whichever local carrier gives the best signal instead of locking you to one partner network the way a lot of single-carrier eSIMs do. We haven't independently measured the switching in the field, so treat it as Yesim's own claim rather than something we've verified.
  </p>

  <!-- Codes -->
  <div class="content-box content-box--tan">
    <h3>Active codes</h3>
    <ul>
      {% for code in provider.codes %}
      {% if not code.isInvalid %}
      <li><strong>{{ code.code }}</strong>: {{ code.discount | lower }}</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:#63553F;">If a code doesn't apply at checkout, refresh the cart or try a private window, then retry.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Real operational note -->
  <h2>The Refund Policy Is Better Than Most eSIM Apps</h2>
  <p>
    Yesim advertises a 30-day money-back guarantee on unused plans, refundable through their own policy rather than just for eSIMs that fail to activate. Most providers on this site, including Yesim's own cheaper competitors, only refund a plan that never connected in the first place and treat any activated plan as final. That's worth knowing if you tend to buy ahead of a trip and aren't sure you'll actually use the plan.
  </p>
  <p>
    The tradeoff is price. Yesim sits in our "Expensive" bracket: day-based plans run from roughly $1.56 to $31 depending on destination, noticeably above what <a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a> or <a href="/airhub/">Airhub</a> charge for comparable coverage. You're paying for the refund flexibility and the Pay & Fly balance model, not for the cheapest rate per GB.
  </p>

  <!-- How to -->
  <h2>Apply a Yesim Code in 3 Steps</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <ol>
      <li>Copy <strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong></li>
      <li>Pick a country, regional, or Pay & Fly balance plan for your destination on Yesim</li>
      <li>Paste the code in the promo field at checkout and confirm the price drop before paying</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="content-note">Discount shows before payment is completed.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Decision help -->
  <h2>Is Yesim the Right Pick for Your Trip</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--good">
      <h3>Good fit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You travel often and want a data balance that rolls over instead of a plan that expires between trips</li>
        <li>You want the option of a real refund if you buy ahead and end up not needing the plan</li>
        <li>You'd rather pay in dollars for data used than track a fixed GB allowance</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--alt">
      <h3>Consider alternatives</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You just want the cheapest rate for a single trip: check <a href="/airhub/">Airhub</a> or <a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a> first</li>
        <li>You want unlimited data with no usage tracking at all: see <a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Savings examples -->
  <h2>What the Discount Looks Like</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <ul>
      <li>United States 1 day at $8.40 &rarr; 20% off saves $1.68</li>
      <li>Japan 7 days at $19.80 &rarr; 20% off saves $3.96</li>
      <li>UAE 1 day at $7.70 &rarr; 20% off saves $1.54</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="content-note">{{ provider.primaryCode }} only applies to your first Yesim purchase. After that, <strong>WELCOMETOYESIM</strong> (15% off) and <strong>TRAVELFREE</strong> (a flat &euro;3 off) are the codes worth trying on repeat orders.</p>
  </div>

  <p>
    For eSIM device compatibility, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <div class="content-cta">
    <h2>Use the Code at Checkout</h2>
    <p>Copy <code>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</code> then paste in the promo field</p>
    <p>{{ primary.discount | lower }} on your first Yesim eSIM.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Yesim Promo Code FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What is the best code right now</h3>
      <p><strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong>: {{ primary.discount | lower }}, for first-time buyers. Returning customers should try <strong>WELCOMETOYESIM</strong> or <strong>TRAVELFREE</strong> instead.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What is a Pay &amp; Fly plan</h3>
      <p>It's Yesim's balance-based option: you top up a dollar amount rather than buying a fixed block of GB, priced from $1.10/GB, and unused balance carries over to your next trip instead of expiring.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I get a refund if I don't use the plan</h3>
      <p>Yesim advertises a 30-day money-back guarantee on unused plans, which is a step further than most eSIM providers on this site that only refund a plan that never connected at all. Refunds still run through Yesim's own policy, not through us.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is Yesim the cheapest option</h3>
      <p>No. Yesim sits in our "Expensive" price bracket. If price per GB is your main concern, check Airhub or Holafly before buying.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does Yesim include a phone number</h3>
      <p>No. It's data-only, like most eSIMs on this site. Voice calls run over apps like WhatsApp or Viber using the data connection.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

